{"step_index":44,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-10T07:49:40Z","content":"Good, 431 lines total. Now let me combine all three into one final print-ready artifact with a diagrams section at the end.","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"$ch1 = Get-Content \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\56cfa12c-2639-4af2-b68d-7a6a362979cc\\ECM_Chapter1_StudyGuide.md\" -Raw; $ch2 = Get-Content \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\0c57eb41-b6b1-4508-a0f2-a32e00576b8d\\ECM_Chapter2_StudyGuide.md\" -Raw; $ch3 = Get-Content \"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\2a9dbf06-360a-4549-87fe-f576409e10a3\\ECM_Chapter3_StudyGuide.md\" -Raw; $header = @\"\n# Energy Conservation and Management (BE05019021)\n## Complete Study Guide for Mid-Sem (30 Marks)\n### Exam: 10/09/2026 | Chapters 1-3 | All Tier 1, Tier 2, and Key Tier 3 Topics\n\n---\n\n\"@; $diagrams = @\"\n\n---\n\n# DIAGRAMS NEEDED (Questions with Drawings)\n\nThe following questions need hand-drawn diagrams. Search for these on Google Images or your textbook.\n\n## 1. CDM Project Cycle Flowchart\n**Question:** Write a note on CDM methodology and its project cycle with neat sketch. (7 marks)\n\n**What to draw:** A vertical or circular flowchart with 7 boxes connected by arrows:\nProject Design (PDD) -> National Approval (DNA) -> Validation (DOE) -> Registration (CDM Executive Board) -> Monitoring (Project Developer) -> Verification (Second DOE) -> CER Issuance (CDM Executive Board)\n\n**Google search:** ``CDM project cycle flowchart diagram``\n\n## 2. Ball Float Steam Trap\n**Question:** Explain ball float steam trap with neat sketch. (Part of 7-mark steam trap question)\n\n**What to draw:** Cross-section showing: trap body (chamber), inlet pipe on left, outlet pipe on right-bottom, a hollow ball floating on condensate, valve seat connected to the ball by a lever, vent at top for air release.\n\n**How it works in the diagram:** When condensate fills the body, ball rises and opens valve. When steam enters, ball drops and closes valve.\n\n**Google search:** ``ball float steam trap working diagram``\n\n## 3. Inverted Bucket Steam Trap\n**Question:** Explain inverted bucket steam trap with neat sketch. (Part of 7-mark steam trap question)\n\n**What to draw:** Cross-section showing: trap body, an inverted bucket (open end down) inside the body, inlet pipe entering at bottom into the bucket, outlet valve at top connected to bucket by a lever, outlet pipe.\n\n**How it works in the diagram:** Steam enters bucket from below, bucket floats up, closes valve. Steam condenses, bucket sinks, valve opens, condensate drains out.\n\n**Google search:** ``inverted bucket steam trap working diagram``\n\n## 4. Boiler Efficiency Losses Breakdown (Optional)\n**Question:** This is not a specific PYQ diagram, but drawing a pie chart or bar chart of boiler losses helps in the indirect method question.\n\n**What to draw:** A simple pie chart showing typical losses for an oil-fired boiler:\n- Dry flue gas loss: 7-8%\n- Hydrogen in fuel: 7%\n- Moisture losses: 0.5%\n- Radiation: 2%\n- Useful heat output: 82-83%\n\n---\n\n*End of Study Guide*\n\"@; $combined = $header + $ch1 + \"`n`n---`n`n\" + $ch2 + \"`n`n---`n`n\" + $ch3 + $diagrams; [System.IO.File]::WriteAllText(\"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\959a947c-6b1c-457d-b2a6-900bb164db70\\ECM_COMPLETE_StudyGuide.md\", $combined, [System.Text.Encoding]::UTF8); Write-Output \"Combined file created successfully\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\renu5\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\959a947c-6b1c-457d-b2a6-900bb164db70","WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Combining all chapters","toolSummary":"Final study guide assembly"}}]}
